{#
  /{uri}.md — one page as Markdown, for an agent that wants the text of a page without
  its HTML. The homepage is /index.md. Built by _md.twig's page(), the same macro
  /llms-full.txt is made of.

  A SEPARATE ADDRESS, NOT CONTENT NEGOTIATION. Serving Markdown at the page's own URL
  for `Accept: text/markdown` would put two bodies behind one URL, and Cloudflare
  caches by URL without varying on Accept — one agent's request could land Markdown in
  the cache for every visitor after it.

  Only the sections _md.twig lists have one; any other URI 404s — a VIP door in
  particular must never come back as text.

  text/markdown (RFC 7763): this is what an agent asks for by name. noindex for the
  reason llms.txt has it — the HTML page is the one to rank.
#}
{%- import '_views/feeds/_md' as md -%}
{%- set uri = path == 'index' ? '__home__' : path -%}
{%- set entry = craft.entries().uri(uri).section(md.sections()|split(',')).status('live').one() -%}
{%- if not entry -%}
    {%- exit 404 -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- header "Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8" -%}
{%- header "X-Robots-Tag: noindex" -%}
{% autoescape false %}
{% apply replace('/\\n{3,}/', "\n\n", true) %}
{{ md.page(entry, 1)|trim }}
{% endapply %}
{% endautoescape %}
